    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="0429350c-e612-5b47-b3b8-7109e920677a" activityNameId="8e4f2d23-0c13-59e8-87db-cfa04eb003bf" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Transport, natural gas, offshore pipeline, long distance</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Transport, natural gas, offshore pipeline, long distance
Infrastructure requirements are based on estimated standard capacity.;
e405bfbc-e2e6-3766-8dff-b7dc1c6ab64c
This dataset describes the energy consumption and the emissions linked to the transport of Nigerian natural gas in an offshore pipeline.
Location:  The data for emissions are based on European data and for energy requirements on German data.
Technology: Long-distance transport offshore with  average compressor station.
Time period: The data for emissions is from 2006, the data for energy requirements from 2001
Production volume: 0 million tons of directly imported natural gas globally in 2019.
Sampling: Literature.
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_e405bfbc-e2e6-3766-8dff-b7dc1c6ab64c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
